.TH TANNOY 1 "2026-11-11" "tannoy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tannoy \- now playing for waybar, with cover art and a drawer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tannoy
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tannoy
tracks every MPRIS player on the session bus from D\-Bus signals and shows
the one you picked, or the one that most recently started playing, in a
waybar module with its cover.
Clicking the module opens a drawer
.RB ( tannoy\-board )
with the cover, a scrub bar, the controls and the players.
While do not disturb is on (swaync, dunst or mako) or the screen is shared
(Hyprland), titles and covers stay off the screen.
.PP
One binary is the daemon, the waybar module and the command line.
Commands start the daemon when it is not running, except
.BR art ,
.B status
and
.BR hide .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B play\-pause
Play or pause the picked player.
.TP
.BR next ", " previous
Skip to the next or previous track.
.TP
.BI seek " secs"
Seek relative with a sign
.RB ( +5 ", " \-15 )
or to a position in seconds
.RB ( 90 ).
.TP
.B raise
Bring the picked player's window forward, for players that offer it.
.TP
.BI pick " player"
Send the bar, the media keys and the drawer to this player: a bus name
key, suffix or name, whole or as a prefix
.RB ( spotify ", " chrome ).
.B auto
follows whichever player started playing last.
The pick survives the player restarting.
.TP
.BR toggle " [" \-\-center ]
Open or close the drawer from the bar icon under the cursor (Hyprland), or
centered.
.TP
.BR show " [" \-\-center "], " hide
Open or close the drawer.
.TP
.B bar
The waybar
.B custom
module: prints a JSON line whenever the bar should change.
Its classes are
.BR playing ", " paused ", " hidden ", " stopped " or " offline ,
plus
.B with\-art
while the image module shows a cover.
.TP
.B art
The cover's path, for a waybar
.B image
module.
Prints a path that never exists when there is no cover, which hides the
module.
Answers within 400 ms and never starts the daemon.
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
What is playing, on which players; with
.BR \-\-json ,
the daemon's snapshot.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the session bus, the notification daemon, screen sharing, waybar,
the art signal and the drawer.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the daemon and the drawer.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " help
Print the version or the usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tannoy/config.toml
The config; every key is optional.
A typo falls back to the defaults and the drawer and
.B doctor
say what is wrong.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tannoy/style.css
Overrides any part of the drawer's look.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tannoy/
The picked player
.RI ( state.json )
and the logs
.RI ( daemon.log ", " board.log ),
each moved to
.I .1
past 1 MB.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/tannoy/art/
Cached covers.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tannoy/
The daemon's socket and lock.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR TANNOY_CONFIG_DIR ", " TANNOY_STATE_DIR ", " TANNOY_CACHE_DIR ", " TANNOY_RUNTIME_DIR
Move each place above, for a development build next to an installed one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error (the message says why).
.B tannoy daemon
exits with 75 when another daemon is already running.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR waybar (5),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/NathanielInman/tannoy
